Experiment 24 (render-mode verdict histogram) - NOT FOR COMMIT. One call per render
pass records the verdict of the sysmem/gmem decision, whether HW binning would have
been used, and the reason string the driver keeps for itself; a histogram of those
is printed once per second on stderr while TU_DBG_RM_HIST=1.

Purpose. Queue 22 of docs/plan-next-checks.md and journal 40.15. Every render-mode
measurement in this repository forces a mode and measures the consequence -
TU_DEBUG=gmem with and without forcebin (journal 40.10, and 40.16 where that costs a
third of the fps), TU_DEBUG=sysmem (40.20, no change) - and none has recorded what
the autotuner decides by itself. The reason for a pass is computed and stored in
tu_cmd_buffer::state.rp.force_render_mode_reason (tu_cmd_buffer.cc:1424-1487) and
never logged, only traced, so "the driver chose sysmem because of X" is not a
quantity anyone can count today. This rig makes it one: passes per verdict and
reason, over the steady stretch of a run, next to the fps of the same run.

Why a separate gate. TU_DEBUG bits are a fixed set and every recorded measurement
names its mask; a new bit would silently change what a recorded mask means. So the
rig has its own environment variable, TU_DBG_RM_HIST=1, and without it the added
code is one comparison against a cached flag per render pass and one call per submit
that returns. The printing reuses the once-per-second slot in queue_submit() that
tu_dbg_log_gmem_load_store_skips() (tu_util.cc:593-642) already uses.

The reason strings are literals owned by the driver, so the table stores the pointer
and compares it by identity: no copies, no allocation, no lifetime question.

Rollback: git apply -R experiments/exp-24-render-mode-histogram.patch - the patch
touches exactly tu_cmd_buffer.cc, tu_queue.cc, tu_util.cc and tu_util.h, and nothing
else in those files (tu_cmd_buffer.cc also carries 0013 and 0014 in an uncommitted
tree, so revert this patch and never git checkout, AGENTS.md).

Provenance: written into ../mesa27-src on 22.11 as part of journal 40.15 and left
applied there; saved as this patch file on 23.11 while the tree was inventoried for
the 0014 A/B (queue 16), which is what found the rig in the tree with no patch file
next to it. Neither built nor run: queue 22 is still open, and this file exists so
that the rig can be reverted, carried into a build tree, or dropped.

